└──────┴─────────┴────────┴──────────────────┴────────────────┴───┴──────────────────────┘
Rank order: higher scores first (default). Scores remain in their original 
units.
'not separated: ranks' lists only other models whose paired test has 
Holm-adjusted p >= 0.05. Gaps are preserved; '-' means none. Non-significance 
does not establish equivalence. The overlapping groups remain in --json.
Scoring checks reject conflicting recorded names or configurations on shared 
questions. Missing declarations remain unchecked; matching declarations do not 
verify scorer code or unrecorded settings.
                               pairwise paired tests (Holm-corrected)                                
┏━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓
┃ A     ┃ B       ┃ shared n ┃ mean diff ┃ test          ┃ p (used) ┃ p (used, Holm) ┃ significant? ┃
┡━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┩
│ wrong │ perfect │        8 │   +1.0000 │ McNemar exact │ 0.007812 │       0.007812 │ yes          │
└───────┴─────────┴──────────┴───────────┴───────────────┴──────────┴────────────────┴──────────────┘
Paired differences have zero estimated variance. The t-test uses p=0 for a 
nonzero difference and p=1 for identical scores by convention; a point interval 
does not establish population certainty. Use the exact McNemar result for binary
pairs.
Correlation is unavailable because at least one score vector is constant.
Variance reduction is unavailable because both score vectors are constant.
'p (used, Holm)' adjusts the selected tests across all tested pairs: clustered t
for dependent questions, exact McNemar for one binary score per shared question,
paired t for continuous scores or repeated-generation means. Groups do not 
establish equivalence.
